{"abstract":"We develop a complexity theory for approximate real computations. We first produce a theory for exact computations but with condition numbers. The input size depends on a condition number, which is not assumed known by the machine. The theory admits deterministic and nondeterministic polynomial time recognizable problems. We prove that P is not NP in this theory if and only if P is not NP in the BSS theory over the reals. Then we develop a theory with weak and strong approximate computations. This theory is intended to model actual numerical computations that are usually performed in floating point arithmetic. It admits classes P and NP and also an NP-complete problem. We relate the P vs NP question in this new theory to the classical P vs NP problem.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"1803.03600","authors":["Gregorio Malajovich","Mike Shub"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-21T07:14:43+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1803.03600.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":52,"pdf_bytes":674730,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"e3d3481a9be4f0cb0cab15b714b3c50c919a8f9a42fdba286710fc5d498f286b","created_at":"2026-08-21T07:14:43+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"c2c40a7d14aca782ea3c6bc893a5f90146f23677e762aa606dac8031f928a4ec","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"A theory of NP-completeness and ill-conditioning for approximate real computations","updated_at":"2026-08-21T07:14:43+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-08787BC80EDC","year":2018}
{"abstract":"This paper describes an application of the Quantum Approximate Optimisation Algorithm (QAOA) to efficiently find approximate solutions for computational problems contained in the polynomially bounded NP optimisation complexity class (NPO PB). We consider a generalisation of the QAOA state evolution to alternating quantum walks and solution-quality-dependent phase shifts, and use the quantum walks to integrate the problem constraints of NPO problems. We apply the recent concept of a hybrid quantum-classical variational scheme to attempt finding the highest expectation value, which contains a high-quality solution. The algorithm is applied to the problem of minimum vertex cover, showing promising results using only a fixed and low number of optimisation parameters.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"1804.08227","authors":["Samuel Marsh","Jingbo Wang"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-21T06:09:31+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.08227.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":19,"pdf_bytes":1750339,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"d342b3ddd0367d3359db7fa5edb40ca7df86ff5dad4f599bd35bd6546537d3ed","created_at":"2026-08-21T06:09:31+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"c778da7a0e0494eabb6aada8c3bab1f455e1fc465ebd7ca159282951fa99dd85","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"A quantum walk assisted approximate algorithm for bounded NP optimisation problems","updated_at":"2026-08-21T06:09:31+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-D0739DE40CED","year":2018}
